# The Mac App test copy's first launch as if on an M1 with an 8-core GPU (DM_TEST_GPU_NAME / DM_TEST_GPU_CORES) on this 2560 x 1440 screen: the
# glue from the chip to the picture for a Mac whose Recommended differs from this one's (t_picrec_cases.h). The 3D runs below 100% with the MetalFX
# 3D pass, and the picture event carries the set the model gives: Native 2560, 3D 75%, environment shadows on, Ultra, Frame Drops lower (about
# 0.31x the M6's GPU, the 75% load at 90% of the estimated capacity, above the 85% line). Pinned from the first run on 2026-11-03. DM_TEST_NO_FG=1: the conventional picture of a chip
# without a frame interpolator, whichever chips those are (the system answers on each device)
name pic_mac_firstboot_m1
requires mac-app
# A background run again since 2026-11-08: the stall that once kept it in front (2 of 20 runs in the background on 2026-11-07) was the GPU hang a
# separate present queue caused on Macs, not the off-screen window (dm/verify/debugging.md, "The GPU hangs for 4 s")
save warlock
timeout 300
env DM_TEST_VIDEO_FIRSTBOOT=1 "DM_TEST_GPU_NAME=Apple M1" DM_TEST_GPU_CORES=8 DM_TEST_NO_FG=1 DM_GAME_SEED=305419896

expect main_menu timeout=120
enter_game
sleep 6
system_quit
check no_red
check no_red_log
check event picture how=first mode=1 res=3 up=1 aa=1 aniso=3 color=1 s3d=2 envsh=1 shq=2 fg=0 envd=1
check log_has "frame interpolator supported: no"
check log_has "→ Recommended Native 2560, 3D 75%, environment shadows on, shadows Ultra, Frame Drops lower"
check event scale3d pct=75
check event mfx who=3d op=build
check no_event mfx who=pres op=build
